/*!
\page page_strichpid StRichPid

\brief \ref page_strichpid "StRichPid" — per-species RICH PID hypothesis with ring statistics.

\section strichpid_overview Overview
StRichPid stores the Cherenkov ring statistics for a single particle species
hypothesis (pion, kaon, or proton). Ring quantities are provided in two forms:
\e total (full geometric ring) and \e truncated (after a constant pad-plane
area cut that equalises acceptance across species). The class also holds the
associated photon hits and per-photon geometry records
(\ref page_strichphotoninfo "StRichPhotonInfo").
Multiple StRichPid objects are owned by
\ref page_strichpidtraits "StRichPidTraits".

\section strichpid_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code
TObject
└── StObject
    └── StRichPid
\endcode

\section strichpid_members Data Members
| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| StParticleDefinition* | mParticleType | Particle species (transient) |
| Int_t | mParticleNumber | PDG-encoded particle number |
| StPtrVecRichHit | mAssociatedHits | Photon hits on this ring (not owned) |
| StSPtrVecRichPhotonInfo | mPhotonInfo | Per-photon geometry records |
| StThreeVectorD | mMipResidual | MIP-to-ring-centre residual |
| Float_t | mTotalAzimuth | Full-ring azimuthal coverage (rad) |
| Float_t | mTotalArea | Full-ring pad-plane area |
| UShort_t | mTotalHits | Photon hits on full ring |
| Float_t | mTotalDensity | Photon density on full ring |
| Float_t | mTruncatedAzimuth | Truncated azimuthal coverage (rad) |
| Float_t | mTruncatedArea | Truncated pad-plane area |
| UShort_t | mTruncatedHits | Photon hits after area cut |
| Float_t | mTruncatedDensity | Photon density after area cut |
| Float_t | mConstantAreaCut | Constant pad-plane area cut value |
| UInt_t | mFlags | PID status flag bit field |

\section strichpid_methods Key Methods
| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| StParticleDefinition* getRingType() const | Particle species definition |
| int getParticleNumber() const | PDG-encoded particle number |
| StThreeVectorD getMipResidual() const | MIP-to-ring-centre residual |
| float getTotalAzimuth() const | Full-ring azimuthal coverage (rad) |
| float getTotalArea() const | Full-ring pad-plane area |
| unsigned short getTotalHits() const | Photon hits on full ring |
| float getTotalDensity() const | Photon density on full ring |
| float getTruncatedAzimuth() const | Truncated azimuthal coverage (rad) |
| float getTruncatedArea() const | Truncated pad-plane area |
| unsigned short getTruncatedHits() const | Photon hits after area cut |
| float getTruncatedDensity() const | Photon density after area cut |
| float getConstantAreaCut() const | Constant-area cut value |
| void setConstantAreaCut(float) | Set constant-area cut |
| const StPtrVecRichHit& getAssociatedRichHits() const | Photon hits on this ring |
| void addHit(StRichHit*) | Add a photon hit |
| const StSPtrVecRichPhotonInfo& getPhotonInfo() | All per-photon geometry records |
| StRichPhotonInfo* getPhotonInfo(int) | Per-photon geometry at index |
| void addPhotonInfo(StRichPhotonInfo*) | Append a photon geometry record |
| bool isSet(StRichPidFlag) const | Test a PID flag bit |
| void setBit(StRichPidFlag) | Set a PID flag bit |
| void unSetBit(StRichPidFlag) | Clear a PID flag bit |

\section strichpid_example Usage Example
\code{.cpp}
StRichPid* pionPid = rpt->getPid(StPionPlus::instance());
if (pionPid) {
    unsigned short n = pionPid->getTruncatedHits();
    float density    = pionPid->getTruncatedDensity();
}
\endcode

\section strichpid_related Related Classes
\ref page_strichpidtraits "StRichPidTraits" — parent object holding all species hypotheses. \n
\ref page_strichphotoninfo "StRichPhotonInfo" — per-photon geometry attached to each hypothesis. \n
\ref page_strichhit "StRichHit" — photon hits referenced by this hypothesis.
*/
